meta {
  name: Send a direct message
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/messages
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  ~Idempotency-Key: replace-with-a-unique-key
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "to": "/acme/john",
    "body": "Your laptop is ready for pickup at the front desk.",
    "thread_title": "Onboarding"
  }
}

docs {
  Sends a direct message **as the key's `send_as` org agent mailbox** to a member or agent mailbox of the same org. It takes the normal hosted direct path: the recipient's blocks, org rules, inbox policy, filters and quotas all apply. Rooms are end-to-end encrypted and cannot be posted to with a key (`409 room_encrypted`); see the guide "Post build results into a room".

  Scope: `messages:send`.

  Errors: `bad_request` (400), `unauthorized` (401), `ip_not_allowed` (403), `insufficient_scope` (403), `forbidden` (403), `recipient_not_in_org` (403), `not_admitted` (403), `feature_disabled` (404), `room_encrypted` (409), `org_inactive` (409), `org_read_only` (409), `idempotency_conflict` (409), `payload_too_large` (413), `rate_limited` (429), `store_error` (500).
}
